 Returns `this` (the instance).
 
-#### .onEmpty()
+#### .onEmpty(options?)
 
 Returns a promise that settles when the queue becomes empty.
 
 Can be called multiple times. Useful if you for example add additional items at a later time.
 
-#### .onIdle()
+Accepts an optional `{signal: AbortSignal}` to cancel this wait. Aborting rejects with exactly `signal.reason` and leaves queued and running tasks unaffected. An already-aborted signal rejects even if the queue is already empty. Listeners for this wait are removed when it settles; other waits and listeners are unaffected.
+
+#### .onIdle(options?)
 
 Returns a promise that settles when the queue becomes empty, and all promises have completed; `queue.size === 0 && queue.pending === 0`.
 
 The difference with `.onEmpty` is that `.onIdle` guarantees that all work from the queue has finished. `.onEmpty` merely signals that the queue is empty, but it could mean that some promises haven't completed yet.
 
+Accepts the same optional `{signal}` as `.onEmpty()`, for example `await queue.onIdle({signal: controller.signal})`. An already-aborted signal rejects with `signal.reason` even if the queue is already idle. Omitting options preserves the usual waiting behavior for both methods.
+
 #### .onSizeLessThan(limit)
 
 Returns a promise that settles when the queue size is less than the given limit: `queue.size < limit`.
